  "besouro-rola-bosta": ["Dung beetle", "Scarab beetle that uses organic matter and contributes to nutrient cycling.", "Compact body, legs adapted for digging and strong jaws.", "Grasslands, open woods and soils with organic matter available.", "Finds resources by smell, then shapes and rolls small balls of material.", "Organic material and the droppings of vertebrates.", ["Burying the resource improves the incorporation of nutrients into the soil.", "Its activity varies with moisture and temperature."], "South America, with records in Brazilian environments.", "Recycles nutrients, aerating the soil and dispersing seeds present in the organic material."],
